1
00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:05,980
=The Cruel Tribunal=
=Episode 7=

2
00:01:07,160 --> 00:01:09,440
How long have you and the Second Prince

3
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:11,080
been seeing each other?

4
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:15,320
We haven't.

5
00:01:22,360 --> 00:01:23,720
Well, we have

6
00:01:23,840 --> 00:01:25,440
met a few times.

7
00:01:30,520 --> 00:01:31,640
From today onward,

8
00:01:32,160 --> 00:01:33,880
you are not to leave the residence.

9
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:35,240
As for His Highness,

10
00:01:35,360 --> 00:01:37,160
I'll send someone to apologize in person

11
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:38,440
and put an end to this for you.

12
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:40,080
Why don't you want

13
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:42,240
me to be with Songpiao?

14
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:43,960
Every time we talk about this,

15
00:01:43,960 --> 00:01:45,360
we end up arguing.

16
00:01:46,040 --> 00:01:48,080
But I like Songpiao.

17
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:54,760
Did I ask for your opinion?

18
00:01:55,120 --> 00:01:57,360
How you feel about the Second Prince

19
00:01:57,680 --> 00:01:58,600
doesn't matter.

20
00:01:59,040 --> 00:02:00,880
How the Second Prince feels about you

21
00:02:01,120 --> 00:02:01,990
doesn't matter either.

22
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:03,640
Marriage is no trivial matter.

23
00:02:10,480 --> 00:02:11,480
Your marriage

24
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:13,400
is not yours to decide.

25
00:02:21,390 --> 00:02:22,800
Keep a close eye on the Young Lady.

26
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,520
If she runs off again,

27
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:26,000
I'll hold you responsible.

28
00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:29,120
(Rousang.)

29
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:32,240
(Becoming a prince's consort
is your duty to the family.)

30
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:34,320
(Songpiao can never become king.)

31
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:37,080
(This is a sacrifice you must make.)

32
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:39,600
(One day, you'll understand.)

33
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:42,640
(Love is worthless
in the face of power.)

34
00:02:43,360 --> 00:02:44,400
(Don't blame me.)

35
00:02:51,560 --> 00:02:52,280
Mother.

36
00:02:52,370 --> 00:02:54,010
Have you heard

37
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:55,990
about the enemy forces
rising in the north?

38
00:02:56,120 --> 00:02:57,380
The unrest on the northern frontier?

39
00:02:57,760 --> 00:02:58,920
Yes, I have.

40
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:01,840
Dark clouds are gathering
over the realm once more.

41
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:04,840
The people will again
suffer the ravages of war.

42
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:09,160
But your father is gravely ill

43
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:10,440
and confined to his bed.

44
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:12,680
Now, every burden

45
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:14,960
rests on my shoulders alone.

46
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:18,440
But how can I simply stand by

47
00:03:18,440 --> 00:03:20,240
and watch this great realm fall to ruin?

48
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:22,240
I am willing
to lead the army into battle

49
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:24,360
and put down the rebellion.

50
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:25,200
No.

51
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:28,800
You are my own flesh and blood.

52
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:30,930
If you go to the northern frontier,

53
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:32,290
you'll face untold dangers,

54
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:34,310
and whether you live
or die is uncertain.

55
00:03:35,280 --> 00:03:36,800
How could I bear to send you

56
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:38,520
into such peril?

57
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,700
I understand how much
you worry about me.

58
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:43,960
I too wish I could remain by your side.

59
00:03:44,640 --> 00:03:46,360
But as a member of the royal family,

60
00:03:46,640 --> 00:03:49,200
while the people of this realm
are suffering so greatly,

61
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:51,160
I must step forward.

62
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:53,840
Even if I may never return
from this campaign,

63
00:03:54,560 --> 00:03:55,080
I

64
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:57,000
will not shrink back in the slightest.

65
00:03:58,160 --> 00:03:59,800
Even if it costs me my life,

66
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:03,240
I must fight

67
00:04:04,560 --> 00:04:05,520
for this realm.

68
00:04:06,320 --> 00:04:07,120
No.

69
00:04:12,320 --> 00:04:14,760
Let me think it over some more.

70
00:04:15,480 --> 00:04:17,800
I'm sure I can find a better way.

71
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:18,600
Mother.

72
00:04:19,200 --> 00:04:20,400
Don't hesitate any longer.

73
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:22,080
The sooner we set out,

74
00:04:22,080 --> 00:04:23,500
the better our chances of victory.

75
00:04:24,240 --> 00:04:25,280
I am going

76
00:04:25,840 --> 00:04:27,720
to defend this realm

77
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:29,680
and keep its people safe.

78
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:32,480
Even if I die on the battlefield,

79
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:33,920
I

80
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:35,760
will have died for a worthy cause.

81
00:04:39,760 --> 00:04:40,560
My son.

82
00:04:41,680 --> 00:04:43,360
You must come back alive.

83
00:04:44,840 --> 00:04:45,920
I'll be waiting for you.

84
00:04:47,440 --> 00:04:49,480
The whole realm
will be waiting for you too.

85
00:04:52,620 --> 00:04:55,620
(Guaranteed Win Legal House)

86
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:01,000
(These two crosses)

87
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:03,480
(don't look like Chinese characters.)

88
00:05:04,080 --> 00:05:06,040
(What could they mean?)

89
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:09,000
He Dang.

90
00:05:09,120 --> 00:05:09,760
Young Lady.

91
00:05:09,920 --> 00:05:10,600
Come here.

92
00:05:12,320 --> 00:05:14,120
Do you know what
these two characters mean?

93
00:05:14,760 --> 00:05:15,360
Well, I...

94
00:05:15,380 --> 00:05:17,280
I've never attended
a day of school in my life.

95
00:05:17,300 --> 00:05:18,800
I only recognize
the words for rice, flour, and oil.

96
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:19,880
Don't laugh at me,

97
00:05:19,880 --> 00:05:21,760
but I can't even write my own name.

98
00:05:24,080 --> 00:05:25,640
Why are they beating the drums outside?

99
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:27,360
When I went
to buy groceries this morning,

100
00:05:27,360 --> 00:05:28,640
I heard there's another rebellion
on the northern frontier

101
00:05:28,640 --> 00:05:29,870
and troops are being sent to fight.

102
00:05:29,880 --> 00:05:30,600
They say

103
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:31,800
the army is setting out today.

104
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:38,280
Right.

105
00:05:38,280 --> 00:05:39,440
Rousang has been to school.

106
00:05:39,440 --> 00:05:40,600
She'll definitely know.

107
00:05:41,280 --> 00:05:42,080
He Dang.

108
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:43,320
Keep an eye on the shop. I'm going out.

109
00:05:43,320 --> 00:05:44,120
All right.

110
00:06:00,300 --> 00:06:02,020
(Prince Luan's Residence)

111
00:06:03,040 --> 00:06:04,150
Prince Luan has given orders.

112
00:06:04,160 --> 00:06:05,700
Miss Rousang is not receiving visitors.

113
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:08,800
Do you know what this is?

114
00:06:09,440 --> 00:06:10,240
What's that?

115
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:12,000
Leave now.

116
00:06:12,280 --> 00:06:13,400
Or we'll deal with you.

117
00:06:14,080 --> 00:06:14,960
Get going!

118
00:06:18,640 --> 00:06:19,520
Fine, I'm leaving.

119
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:20,680
What's the big deal?

120
00:06:24,320 --> 00:06:25,280
(Something's not right.)

121
00:06:25,640 --> 00:06:27,360
(Something must have happened.)

122
00:06:27,760 --> 00:06:28,400
(No.)

123
00:06:28,500 --> 00:06:29,760
(I have to get inside and see.)

124
00:06:39,320 --> 00:06:40,120
Rousang.

125
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:44,240
Rousang.

126
00:06:44,720 --> 00:06:45,920
It's Xiaobai.

127
00:06:46,160 --> 00:06:46,960
Rousang.

128
00:06:50,960 --> 00:06:52,000
Xiaobai.

129
00:06:52,600 --> 00:06:54,560
How did you get onto the roof?

130
00:06:58,240 --> 00:06:59,160
Come on. Slowly.

131
00:06:59,160 --> 00:07:00,760
They wouldn't let me see you,

132
00:07:00,770 --> 00:07:02,640
so I had no choice
but to climb over the wall.

133
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:05,000
By the way,

134
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:07,580
help me figure out
what these two characters mean.

135
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:11,760
These two characters...

136
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:13,160
Xiaobai,

137
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:14,840
who wrote this to you?

138
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:17,080
Never mind that for now.

139
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:18,360
Just tell me what it means.

140
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:21,800
These two characters mean

141
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:22,880
there's only you.

142
00:07:23,160 --> 00:07:24,320
Not one is you,

143
00:07:24,440 --> 00:07:25,680
yet not one isn't you.

144
00:07:26,160 --> 00:07:27,480
It can also mean,

145
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:28,880
"I like you."

146
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:30,080
Just like

147
00:07:30,080 --> 00:07:31,960
the spring breeze
traveling a thousand miles,

148
00:07:32,100 --> 00:07:33,440
never asking when it will return.

149
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:36,280
What did you say?

150
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:38,000
So,

151
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:41,040
who exactly wrote this to you?

152
00:07:44,400 --> 00:07:45,520
Please, Xiaobai,

153
00:07:45,520 --> 00:07:46,960
just tell me.

154
00:07:47,880 --> 00:07:48,840
Sizhou.

155
00:07:54,680 --> 00:07:55,520
What's wrong?

156
00:07:57,680 --> 00:07:59,320
Sizhou

157
00:08:00,160 --> 00:08:01,840
is about to lead the army into battle

158
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:03,840
against the enemy forces.

159
00:08:03,850 --> 00:08:05,180
He's leading the army into battle?

160
00:08:05,280 --> 00:08:06,360
Why?

161
00:08:06,680 --> 00:08:07,760
Because...

162
00:08:08,440 --> 00:08:10,000
Tell me!

163
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:11,480
Sizhou

164
00:08:11,640 --> 00:08:13,640
is the First Prince of Bojue Kingdom.

165
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:16,360
That jerk!

166
00:08:21,480 --> 00:08:22,520
Your Highness.

167
00:08:22,680 --> 00:08:23,560
The army has

168
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:24,550
assembled outside the city

169
00:08:24,560 --> 00:08:25,520
and awaits your command.

170
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:28,400
Brothers!

171
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:29,160
Today,

172
00:08:30,200 --> 00:08:31,600
we gather here

173
00:08:32,280 --> 00:08:34,920
before marching to the battlefield
to face the enemy forces.

174
00:08:35,760 --> 00:08:37,000
Behind us

175
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:38,840
are our homeland

176
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:41,600
and the earnest hopes of our families.

177
00:08:42,560 --> 00:08:44,080
The armor we wear

178
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:46,520
carries our duty to protect them.

179
00:08:46,880 --> 00:08:48,200
The enemy has invaded our borders,

180
00:08:48,210 --> 00:08:49,240
burning, killing, and plundering,

181
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:50,320
committing every evil imaginable.

182
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:51,520
Can we tolerate this?

183
00:08:51,840 --> 00:08:52,600
- No!
- No!

184
00:08:52,680 --> 00:08:53,520
- No!
- No!

185
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:54,360
- No!
- No!

186
00:08:54,560 --> 00:08:55,640
I, Sizhou,

187
00:08:56,520 --> 00:08:58,600
will live and die alongside you all.

188
00:08:59,120 --> 00:08:59,840
On this campaign,

189
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:02,440
we will show the enemy

190
00:09:02,760 --> 00:09:04,480
how fiercely the spirit of Bojue's sons

191
00:09:04,920 --> 00:09:06,160
burns within us,

192
00:09:06,520 --> 00:09:08,000
and just how sharp

193
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:09,480
our blades are!

194
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:10,880
On this campaign,

195
00:09:11,640 --> 00:09:13,240
we will crush the enemy camp

196
00:09:13,280 --> 00:09:14,520
and bring glory to our court!

197
00:09:14,560 --> 00:09:15,920
- Return victorious!
- Return victorious!

198
00:09:15,960 --> 00:09:17,200
- Bring glory to our court!
- Bring glory to our court!

199
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:18,400
- Crush the enemy camp!
- Crush the enemy camp!

200
00:09:18,520 --> 00:09:19,800
- Bring glory to our court!
- Bring glory to our court!

201
00:09:19,800 --> 00:09:20,960
- Crush the enemy camp!
- Crush the enemy camp!

202
00:09:20,960 --> 00:09:22,280
- Bring glory to our court!
- Bring glory to our court!

203
00:09:22,340 --> 00:09:24,220
(Commander)
Move out!

204
00:09:27,720 --> 00:09:28,320
(My son.)

205
00:09:29,160 --> 00:09:30,040
(I know)

206
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,600
(that sending you into battle this time)

207
00:09:32,680 --> 00:09:33,840
(means you may not return.)

208
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:35,720
(But only by doing this)

209
00:09:35,780 --> 00:09:37,320
(can you earn the respect of the realm)

210
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,660
(and have a chance
to inherit the throne.)

211
00:09:40,440 --> 00:09:41,520
(This is your destiny.)

212
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:42,960
(Commander)
(And mine as well.)

213
00:09:43,800 --> 00:09:44,880
(Don't blame me.)

214
00:09:47,960 --> 00:09:49,240
Sizhou!

215
00:10:02,280 --> 00:10:03,200
Sizhou.

216
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:14,600
I want you to tell me yourself

217
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:15,960
what these two characters mean.

218
00:10:17,760 --> 00:10:19,080
What do they mean?

219
00:10:20,720 --> 00:10:21,850
I like you.

220
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:28,360
Remember the two wishes you owe me?

221
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:29,800
Of course I do.

222
00:10:31,300 --> 00:10:32,680
I want to use the second one today.

223
00:10:42,720 --> 00:10:43,960
Promise me

224
00:10:44,680 --> 00:10:46,200
you'll come back safe and sound.

225
00:10:54,040 --> 00:10:55,160
I promise.

226
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:27,520
Hyah!

227
00:11:45,840 --> 00:11:47,280
It's time.

228
00:11:48,760 --> 00:11:50,000
- We pledge our loyalty to our lord!
- We pledge our loyalty to our lord!

229
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:51,320
- We would gladly die for you!
- We would gladly die for you!

230
00:11:59,980 --> 00:12:02,580
♪The candle burns down
to its final glow♪

231
00:12:03,540 --> 00:12:05,940
♪Cold fragrance clings to my hem♪

232
00:12:06,580 --> 00:12:08,340
♪You gently smooth my hair♪

233
00:12:08,340 --> 00:12:11,260
♪Yet your gaze drifts far away♪

234
00:12:13,700 --> 00:12:16,140
♪A hidden blade lies beneath your smile♪

235
00:12:16,500 --> 00:12:19,820
♪You turn away
as if nothing has changed♪

236
00:12:20,420 --> 00:12:21,980
♪Step by step, I walk away♪

237
00:12:22,140 --> 00:12:25,460
♪Each step breaks my heart anew♪

238
00:12:28,220 --> 00:12:31,100
♪If fate had not gone astray♪

239
00:12:31,620 --> 00:12:34,700
♪Why leave me
standing alone in the wind?♪

240
00:12:35,140 --> 00:12:37,740
♪We shared one fleeting life together♪

241
00:12:37,740 --> 00:12:41,780
♪Yet all that's left
is warmth upon my fingertips♪

242
00:12:42,020 --> 00:12:45,060
♪I'd melt this night into ink♪

243
00:12:45,460 --> 00:12:48,140
♪And write of every meeting
and every parting♪

244
00:12:48,140 --> 00:12:50,860
♪If next life asks
about the days gone by♪

245
00:12:51,140 --> 00:12:54,100
♪I'll only say that once♪

246
00:12:54,580 --> 00:12:56,340
♪I called your name♪

247
00:13:00,940 --> 00:13:03,180
♪The silent stars hang low♪

248
00:13:04,580 --> 00:13:06,780
♪The river keeps flowing east♪

249
00:13:08,020 --> 00:13:09,940
♪I linger in the old tower♪

250
00:13:10,060 --> 00:13:13,700
♪Waiting for you,
though all is now empty♪

251
00:13:15,020 --> 00:13:17,460
♪This life still owes us a bow♪

252
00:13:18,340 --> 00:13:21,140
♪May the next repay us with a dream♪

253
00:13:21,900 --> 00:13:24,140
♪Beyond here lie
endless mountains and rivers♪

254
00:13:24,140 --> 00:13:30,380
♪I dare not turn for one last look♪

255
00:13:30,660 --> 00:13:33,540
♪If fate had not gone astray♪

256
00:13:34,140 --> 00:13:37,620
♪Why bury this heart beneath the frost?♪

257
00:13:37,620 --> 00:13:40,260
♪We shared one fleeting life together♪

258
00:13:40,260 --> 00:13:44,540
♪Now only fading warmth
remains in my palm♪

259
00:13:44,540 --> 00:13:47,460
♪I'd melt this night into ink♪

260
00:13:47,900 --> 00:13:50,620
♪And paint a winter between your brows♪

261
00:13:50,620 --> 00:13:53,300
♪If we meet again in another life♪

262
00:13:53,620 --> 00:13:56,340
♪Will you believe that tonight♪

263
00:13:57,020 --> 00:13:59,300
♪Was when we first met?♪

264
00:14:00,580 --> 00:14:02,980
♪Will you believe that tonight♪

265
00:14:04,100 --> 00:14:05,860
♪Was when we met for the last time?♪
